{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מזכר עד נקבה תשלחו", :translit "mi'zachar ad nekeivah teshalchu", :gloss "from male even to female you shall send out"} {:he "על גחונך תלך", :translit "al gachonecha telech", :gloss "upon your belly you shall crawl"} {:he "ענבמו ענבי רוש", :translit "anavimo anvei rosh", :gloss "his grapes are grapes of poison"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): sending out from camp parallels banishment from Eden; adjacent parashot of sotah and nazir tied to the sin of Eve and Adam"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that since Adam and Eve sinned through wine, the nazirite refrains from wine to rectify that primordial transgression, reading Deuteronomy 32:32 — 'their grapes are grapes of rosh' — as describing the fruit Adam consumed (Berakhot 40a; Sanhedrin 70a). Genesis 3:14 records the curse that the serpent would crawl on his belly. The Ba'al HaTurim compresses these into reading the three adjacent sections of Numbers — sending out the impure, the sotah, and the nazirite — as a sequence mapping onto Adam, Eve, and the serpent's banishment from Eden.", :sources ["Genesis 3:14" "Genesis 3:23-24" "Deuteronomy 32:32" "Berakhot 40a" "Sanhedrin 70a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ולא יטמאו", :translit "ve'lo yitma'u", :gloss "and they shall not defile"} {:he "ולא יטמאו עוד בית ישראל את שם קדשי", :translit "ve'lo yitma'u od beit yisrael et shem kadshi", :gloss "and the house of Israel shall no longer defile My holy name"} {:he "למען טמא את מקדשי לחלל את שם קדשי", :translit "le'ma'an timei et mikdashai le'chaleil et shem kadshi", :gloss "to defile My sanctuary, to profane My holy name"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ולא יטמאו" "ולא יטמאו"]}], :frame nil}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): sending out from camp parallels banishment from Eden; adjacent parashot of sotah and nazir tied to the sin of Eve and Adam", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2